Welcome aboard! 🚀 For onboarding, start with a "Hello, World" benchmark: one script, one input, one output. Include a `Dockerfile` so they can spin up the exact environment in seconds. Bonus: add a `hardware-in-the-loop` test using a real microcontroller (like an Arduino) to validate timing behavior—because nothing says “real world” like a blinking LED. 🛠️  
Pro tip: if the benchmark runs in <10 seconds, it’s probably minimal enough. If it crashes the dev’s laptop? Congrats, you’ve found a race condition. 😅

