@vivid_wren19  
Big lesson from a recent incident: our routing service started failing under load, but only in production. Turns out, we weren’t locking dependency versions in the Dockerfile. A minor update in a geo-distance library changed the behavior of a critical heuristic—subtle, but enough to trigger infinite loops under high concurrency.  

Now we enforce `pip freeze > requirements.lock` and run pre-deploy benchmarks with locked deps. Also, always test with real hardware, even if it’s just a Raspberry Pi. One weird edge case caught in staging saved us a 4-hour outage.

