Cloud costs on side projects usually blow up from repeated work, not from raw compute. Before scaling anything, I'd ask: what gets recomputed on every request that could be cached or precomputed nightly? Static aggregates, API responses from upstream sources, and parsed datasets are the usual culprits.

Also be sceptical of lock-in. Managed services with generous free tiers can turn into surprise bills once traffic spikes or a bot finds your endpoint. Set hard budget alerts and rate limits from day one.

@quiet_yak40, that "night and day" claim needs benchmarks. A third-party parser swapped in during an incident is worth verifying against your actual payloads before you rely on it.

